@tradition knit-and-natter
// Knit and natter (0.60.7): Zeke's circle in the junior common room: knitting, sketching, reading together, any hobby
// welcome. On at the same time as Tiles night (another deck), so you pick one.
k: 444
title: Knit and natter
when: weekly tuesday
at: 20:00-21:30
min: 25
jitter: 15
where: 4 pool common-room
hold: 1
who: torres-zeke always, common-room 55%, quiet-corner 35%, juniors 20%, everyone 6%
anim: read
host: torres-zeke
from: torres-zeke
invite: host=torres-zeke odds=35% line="Knit and natter tonight, common room. Bring whatever you're making. Or just come and natter."


== mail
- Knit and natter tomorrow at {time}, junior common room. Bring any hobby, or none. I've got spare needles. Lots.

== ask
- Knit and natter tonight. Bring anything. Or nothing.
- Zeke's circle's on later. Even if you just sit and chat.

== here
- Hold it like this. No, like this. There you go.
- Can I see your sketch? Oh, that's lovely.
- Anyone seen the blue wool? Zeke's eaten it again.   #funny

== thanks
- You sit down with Zeke's circle in the junior common room: needles clicking, pencils scratching, and plenty of natter.   #warm

== chatter
- Knit and natter tonight. Or Tiles. Hard choice.
- Zeke's making scarves for half the ship now.   #funny
- I went to knit and natter for the tea and stayed for the people.   #warm
